35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It turns out the monitor readings show a huge disparity—the heaviest user draws four times more than the lightest. Also, those paying a fixed seasonal rate seem much more relaxed about using the heat.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The reconciliation template was a nightmare to fill out, and the other house spends forty minutes just logging readings and doing math by hand. It sounds like a lot of work!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The payment log confirms that payments are often late and disputed, and the monitor readings Benjamin mentioned prove that our usage is indeed very uneven.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The statements show massive swings, from 9,100 yen in August to nearly 30,000 in February. Also, fitting sub-meters would cost 34,000 yen per room plus annual maintenance and installation time.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,"The payment log shows people are late when they're confused, and the cooler notice says some people suffered in the heat just to avoid arguments. It's sad that we feel this way.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, that installation cost is quite steep. Given the disparity in usage I found, we have to decide if paying for meters is worth the peace of mind or if it's too expensive.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"I agree with Benjamin! If it's that expensive and the other house spends so much time on math, maybe we should avoid anything that makes the monthly settle a huge chore.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"It is clear that the current system is causing resentment. If usage is as uneven as the monitor readings suggest, a simple split is unfair, yet the payment log shows that complexity leads to delays.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"The cost of meters is high, but the statements prove that the seasonal swings are the real problem. We can't ignore that some of us are paying nearly triple in winter.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,"I think we should choose something that doesn't make us feel bad or stressed. If people are suffering in the heat just to avoid fighting, the system is already broken.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"If we want to avoid the stress Minato mentioned, the seasonal fixed rate seems promising. It removes the monthly anxiety of a fluctuating bill and the guilt of flicking a switch.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"That sounds way easier than doing a bunch of math every month! If we just agree on a number for the season, we can spend our evenings doing something fun instead.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"A fixed rate would certainly reduce the monthly disputes, but we must ensure the year-end settlement doesn't become a new source of conflict if the actual costs differ significantly.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"I agree with Jonathan. If we use a fixed rate, we need a clear plan for the year-end adjustment so that the winter spikes don't suddenly become an overwhelming burden for anyone.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I just want us to be honest with each other. If we pick a fixed rate, can we promise to be kind when we settle the difference at the end of the year?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I believe we can. The key is that the fixed rate removes the daily tension. If we agree on the logic now, the final adjustment becomes a formality rather than a fight.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm totally on board with that! As long as we don't have to spend hours with a calculator every single month, I think it's the best way to keep everyone happy.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. While a flat split is simple, it ignores the usage disparity we discovered. A seasonal fixed rate balances simplicity with a level of predictability that should ease the tension.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. Given the high cost of meters and the volatility of the bills, a seasonal fixed rate is the most rational compromise to ensure stability and fairness.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I agree too. If everyone feels more relaxed and we can stop worrying about the bills every day, then I think this is the right choice for our home.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
