60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Now that we've discussed the findings, it's time to vote. I vote for Option B: Seasonal Fixed Rate, as it addresses both the usage anxiety and the monthly friction.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,I vote for Option B too! It's the simplest way to make sure we don't spend all our free time doing boring math.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for Option B: Seasonal Fixed Rate. It seems the most effective way to mitigate the resentment caused by uneven usage while avoiding the complexity that leads to payment delays.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,I vote for Option B. It provides the financial predictability I need for the winter months and avoids the prohibitive upfront cost of installing meters.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,I vote for Option B as well. I hope this means we can all be friends again and stop feeling stressed about the money.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
